      "body": "## Problem\n`cargo test` (all targets) in `pkgs/id` does not compile on current main (verified 2026-11-02 on origin/main c91c679b4, worktree for task 6304 / issue #4067 — that change touches only `pkgs/id/src/app_manifest.rs` and its lib tests all pass).\n\nIntegration test targets fail with:\n```\nerror[E0063]: missing field `link` in initializer of `ChainExt`\n  --> tests/documents.rs:101, 117, 375\n  --> tests/tag_claims.rs:258, 268\n  --> tests/bridge_poc.rs:159, 190\n  (also production_ingest, aliases targets fail to compile)\n```\n`pkgs/id/src/chain.rs:99` `ChainExt` gained a `link` field; the integration-test initializers were not updated.\n\n## Evidence\n- `cargo test app_manifest` in pkgs/id: could not compile `id` (test \"documents\"), (test \"tag_claims\"), (test \"bridge_poc\"), (test \"production_ingest\"), (test \"aliases\") — all E0063 above.\n- `cargo test --lib app_manifest`: 12 passed — the lib target is unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance\n- All `pkgs/id` test targets compile again (initializers updated for the `link` field, or the field gains a default the tests can rely on — author's call).\n- `cargo test` in pkgs/id runs the integration suites again.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The pkgs/id integration tests compile on main (the ChainExt initializers name the new link field).\n- The affected integration test target passes in CI on main.\n- No production behavior changes beyond what the compile fix requires.\n",
